---
description: Bash / shell script reliability — strict mode preamble, quoting, traps.
globs: **/*.sh,**/*.bash,**/*.zsh
alwaysApply: false
---

Every script MUST start with:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
IFS=$'\n\t'
```

- ALWAYS quote expansions (`"${VAR}"`, `"$@"`). Prefer `[[ ... ]]` over `[ ... ]`; arithmetic with `(( ... ))`.
- ALWAYS check required commands up front: `command -v jq >/dev/null || { echo "jq required" >&2; exit 1; }`.
- ALWAYS use `mktemp` + `trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT` for cleanup.
- NEVER `eval` interpolated user input. NEVER `curl | bash`. NEVER parse `ls` (use globs or `find -print0 | xargs -0`).
- ALWAYS run `shellcheck` clean (warnings as errors).
